            {
                "post_id": "post_a1f085b8",
                "title": "Wildlife Population Update – Gray Wolf & Red Fox (April 2026 Release)",
                "body": "We are pleased to share the latest approved population figures from our Q1 2026 surveys, released on 2026-04-15.\n\n**Gray Wolf (Canis lupus) — Northern Range**\n- Estimated population: **428 individuals**\n- Dataset: wds_gray_wolf_2026_04_15 (v1.0) | Approved for publication ✓\n\n**Red Fox (Vulpes vulpes) — Northern Range**\n- Estimated population: **1,260 individuals**\n- Dataset: wds_red_fox_2026_04_15 (v1.0) | Approved for publication ✓\n\nBoth datasets have been independently verified as the current approved releases and are sourced from FanaticWildlifeViews.com. These figures reflect surveys conducted during Q1 2026 across the Northern Range and will inform ongoing habitat management and conservation planning efforts.\n\nFor full methodology and raw data, please visit:\n• https://fanaticwildlifeviews.com/datasets/gray-wolf-2026-04-15\n• https://fanaticwildlifeviews.com/datasets/red-fox-2026-04-15",
                "published_at": "2026-11-01T23:11:52.451630Z",
                "channel": "conservation_blog"
            }
